# As many processes as the table holds (roadmap memory.md M4): init starts
# tests/posix/held.c (TEST_POSIX_HELD), which forks children, each waiting
# on a pipe, until a fork is refused. With 256 slots of its own to give
# out, the root refused the 22nd child (E6), the table not yet full; with
# 768 (D8) the table fills first: CHILD_MAX less init and held itself.
program: idle
define: TEST_POSIX_HELD
keys: {wait 250}{wait 250}{wait 250}{wait 250}
match: contains
timeout: 120
---
held: the table full, not the root (CHILD_MAX - 2): yes
held: all reaped
